  "findings": "Rounded kidney leaves on petioles, branching ascending flower stalks with yellow five-sepal flowers; not flat rosette and top hat. Dedicated caltha staged. Current seeds 1, 4 and 7 and every panel in the 36-seed contact sheet were visually inspected. Rounded petioled leaves and ascending branched yellow flower stalks give a low wetland colony. The 17\u201335 cm forms retain varied spread and height. Kidney notches and five individual sepals are only partly represented by the small number of cells. Accepted as a coarse stylized spring source at 25 mm; user endorsement remains separate.",
